<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaykaus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1279</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Izz al-Din Kaykaus II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaykaus II was sultan of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> from 1246, under Mongol overlordship, sharing or disputing the throne with his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-iv">Kilij Arslan IV</a> and Kayqubad II. Pressed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and his rivals, he fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in 1261 and later to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaykaus-ii.jpg" alt="Kaykaus II" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinar_-_Kaya%27us_II,_Qilij_Arslan_IV_and_Kayqubad_II.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
